{
 "format": 1,
 "kind": "sweepercad-asset",
 "name": "Robot",
 "notes": "A little robot, built the way SweeperCAD likes it: think of the object, then of the sweep. Head and body are round shells (a circle swept up, the silhouette drawn as the scale graph). Each boot is two drawings: its plan outline extruded up, KEPT INSIDE its side silhouette swept across the width (an intersect). The visor is a slab cut out of the dome and a dark slab kept inside a 2% smaller dome, so the glass follows the head's curve. Joints are dark pods with a glowing torus (a circle on a circular spine); the neck is a cylinder with a stepped scale graph (ribs); sleeves are rounded squares along a slightly bent spine. Fillets only where the big shells meet - the limbs chain crisp. Three colour groups: shells, dark hardware, lights.",
 "graph": {
